From ea40598a68bab5690e0d08f845e2776ef9be2db9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olivia Lee <olivia.lee@collabora.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:08:28 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] pan/va: fix out-of-bounds read propagating swizzles on pseudo
 instructions

For variable src pseudo instructions (PHI and COLLECT.i32), src info is
not recorded in the info.srcs array. The array is also statically sized,
and there may be more than 4 srcs leading to an out-of-bounds access.

Fixes: 67a662ed058a (pan/bi: Propagate MKVEC.v2i8 and V2X8_TO_V2X16 for replicate swizzle)
Signed-off-by: Olivia Lee <olivia.lee@collabora.com>
Reviewed-by: Eric R. Smith <eric.smith@collabora.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/45650>

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/valhall/va_optimize.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/valhall/va_optimize.c
index 617bc329b8d..8845f461abf 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/valhall/va_optimize.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/valhall/va_optimize.c
@@ -296,6 +296,10 @@ va_propagate_replicate_wide(bi_context *ctx, bi_instr **lut, bi_instr *I)
    struct va_opcode_info info = valhall_opcodes[I->op];
    bool progress = false;
 
+   bool variable_srcs = info.nr_srcs == 0;
+   if (variable_srcs)
+      return false;
+
    bi_foreach_ssa_src(I, s) {
       if (!info.srcs[s].widen)
          continue;
-- 
